styles comfort=practical gossip=guarded refuse=brisk tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# folds a strip of worn cloth until one spotless square shows, keeping the rest of its history inside.

words
oath! = Three ragged hems | A bootful of cold tea
saying! = Fold the story inward | A clean inch can do a job
endfold = the inward fold | my private seam
smallwhite = a clean inch | the pale square
bluerag = a blue thread | an old selvedge
heelwrap = a heel strip | a soft backing
saltfog = a wet white veil | harbour mist
cheeseknob = a hard little heel | the cheese button
teabite = a hot swallow | a steaming lipful
stonewrap = the tool wrap | the stone pocket
walkend = a dry resting place | my turning point
ragmark = a worn corner | the old crease
bootdream = a new sole | a dry tongue
millcloth = a sound strip | the clean scrap

any
opinion merchants against 1 : A seller quoting whole-cloth money for a square of sound rag had best offer a fine reason.
opinion houses mixed 0 : A grand sleeve and a threadbare one can each hide a face that deserves its private moment.
opinion dole for 2 : A dry wrap round a loaf protects the food long after the dole queue has moved.
opinion road for 1 : I'd see the long walking road mended before the grand short cut gets a second sign.
opinion watch mixed 0 : A witness need only give the facts a question actually concerns.
opinion city mixed 0 : Even the best harbour view can be badly let down by the bootsole beneath it.

grown
line greet : Hello. There's a dry inch to stand on. | Come up past the loose rag.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : New face. Wipe your feet before judging the floor. | There's a free patch by my folded cloth.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : First mist gives a plain harbour some manners. | Morning. Still a little white along the water.
line greet.return : Yes, hello. My left ear's still dry. | I heard that quite clearly across the fold.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar voice won't fray my temper today. | You've found the sound side of my morning.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Late. No need to air a whole length of cloth. | Evening. A short quiet word will carry.
line again.open : Back before the crease has set. | Another visitor to this same clean inch.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Take this turning while the mist looks good! | There's a dry view from my side!
line farewell : Walk till your boots have had their money's worth. | Carry one clean corner home.
line farewell.return : I'll fold my bit of silence up again. | Go with the sound side toward the wet.
line react.news : Give me the clean inch of the account. | I can sort the straight part from its fraying edge.
line react.news.new : First thread of that colour I've seen. | New to my small stock of information.
line react.news.known : I've handled a strip cut from that account. | Same old crease running down its middle.
line react.news.doubt : That story's been washed till the useful marks are gone. | Show me the source under that splendid fold.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : A sorrow needn't be spread out for inspection. | I have a clean cloth for you if it's wanted.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : Good. A bright strip in an old grey day. | That's a change worth turning the clean side out for.
line ask.how : Has today rubbed a sore spot anywhere? | Still some sound walking left in your boots?
line answer.how : Fair. Dry inside the collar so far. | Short of money, long enough on feet.
line decline : My spare inch is carrying something I mean to protect. | That would open a fold I'd rather leave closed.
line accept_decline : Then your reasons can stay inside the fold. | No need to air your private account.
line preclose : The next street won't walk itself today. | Time to tuck the strip out of the wet.
line accept_preclose : Go while your boot leather's willing. | Fair enough. Our cloth has a clean edge there.
line thank : That was a kindness you needn't have spent. Thanks. | You've saved the last sound inch.
line deflect_thanks : I only turned the clean bit toward you. | It took no more than one turn of cloth.
line sympathise : Let the sore part stay wrapped today. | I'll keep the staring faces off this corner.
line reassure : Tomorrow may give the fold a sounder face. | There's one patch still bearing weight under us.
line ack : Yes. I'd call that cloth fit for use. | There's sound weave in your argument.
line give.advice : Look inside a boot before blaming the road. | Never unfold a private hurt to amuse a crowd.

scene foldcloth
when topic=work self.job=none self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At rag work I look for the clean inch. Some grand lengths haven't got one left.
b : Is it always on the inside? | What if the outside's fine?
a : Often behind an old fold. That's where rough handling seldom finds it. | Lovely. Then I'm looking for two useful pieces in a single length of rag.

scene toolwrap
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My whetstone travels wrapped. It gets a cleaner lodging than my feet some weeks.
b : Does a stone mind dirt? | Why bother carrying it?
a : The pocket minds the grit. I prefer to keep cheese in a pocket with fewer ambitions. | A cloth tool that can't do its honest work wastes sound material. I look after what earns its place.

scene cheese
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A hard cheese heel makes a neat parcel in my square of cloth. No dripping riddles.
b : What happens to the rind? | Does everything get its own wrap?
a : Goes in the pot when there's one going. I'm not wealthy enough to discard a second flavour. | Anything that would offend my cheese gets a strictly separate residence.

scene stale
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Stale bread wants a day's wages in tea before you can call it a meal.
b : Could you toast it? | Why tea?
a : With fuel available, yes. A cold hearth seldom rises to the invitation. | Broth if I've got it. Dry bread shouldn't send me out buying a list of accompaniments.

scene coldtea
when topic=day self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Cold tea has an air of having been useful to somebody else first.
b : Wouldn't it warm again? | Do you pour it away?
a : If the fire's going. I'd have preferred one decent hot swallow at the start. | I finish it. A grievance can be entirely justified and still drinkable.

scene boots
when topic=travel self.likes=new_boots
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd choose new boots by the inside seam and walk a short circle before admiring the polish.
b : Would you pay more for looks? | Why such a short circle?
a : With my purse? I'd treat a decent sole as decoration enough. | No need for a harbour excursion to find that a stitch is rubbing in precisely the wrong place.

scene longwalk
when topic=pastimes self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long walk lets me turn the same thought until its rough side is out of sight.
b : Do you come to an answer? | Where does your return walk start?
a : If it deserves one. Some things need a fold and no more talking. | Where the ground changes under my feet. I enjoy a different surface on the return.

scene mist
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Dawn mist takes the hard outlines off a wharf. Even a worn coat gets a fine edge in it.
b : Can you see your feet? | Is it the quiet you like?
a : Briefly, between patches. I watch each board fairly closely in any case. | The privacy. An ordinary face can pass without supplying an explanation for it.

scene sawone
when topic=memories
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I once saw a face that belonged to a high place looking thoroughly mortal. Its owner has my silence.
b : Couldn't you at least describe it? | What makes that worth keeping?
a : That's how a description becomes a name before you've got round to finishing it. | Being high up oughtn't to cost a wolf all chance of having a private minute to be unhappy.

scene watchhear
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A strip of cloth can cover a cut. It oughtn't to be pulled off just to prove there's blood.
b : Are we talking about talk? | What if the tale's true?
a : Mostly. The principle works on a real sore place as well. | True facts can still be put to a wretched use. I'd consider the purpose before the telling.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd keep a quiet bit of company for #self.friend# along a road where silence doesn't require a joint explanation.
b : Would you share the road all day? | Doesn't the quiet drag?
a : As far as our roads happen to agree. I like an arrangement with an honest turning place. | Heavy talk drags. A comfortable silence wears almost as well as good leather.

scene wharf
when topic=home self.quarter=wharf
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A strip left loose near the water will begin its own journey sooner than most cargo.
b : Would you go after it? | Why not weigh it down?
a : Only within reach of my hand from solid ground. It's a poor bit of arithmetic to lose a wolf for a rag. | Exactly. A clean little stone in the fold earns its own passage.

scene prayer
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A private minute earns my thanks after a public working day. Even a wet street has those.
b : Why a private one? | Does the cloth come into it?
a : Because I can say what I'm grateful for without supplying anybody else a story. | Occasionally. A used sleeve won't conceal gratitude from the Bright One.

scene cheap
when topic=prices self.wealth=destitute
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I judge a price by the walks it costs. Some fine boots cost more walks than they'd ever give me.
b : Then what would you buy? | Could you save for a pair?
a : A plain pair with a sound lining. There's no sense carrying a seller's vanity on my feet. | I can save the idea at present. It's light enough to carry while I look for a decent bargain.

scene firstfold
when topic=newcomer
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Handle a strange rag by a corner before deciding it's worth the room in a sack.
b : What could be wrong with it? | Why only a corner?
a : A damp inside and splendid dry outer fold. Sellers learn the same folds I know. | It lets me turn the rest of the length open without collecting every stain on my front.

scene hope
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give me one pair of boots able to walk out of a mist and back into it next dawn.
b : No grander wish? | How would you spend that walk?
a : A long comfortable walk seems a fairly grand wish from the patch where I stand. | On the water's edge while the day is still thinking about getting up.

scene marketnews
when topic=news world.news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've had this from #world.news_from#. #world.news#. The wrapping says where it came from.
b : Would you guarantee it? | Why keep the wrapping?
a : I'd guarantee I heard it in that form. My guarantees are properly modest. | A tale with its origin washed off is a rather different parcel.

scene summerland
when topic=land
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One paving stone on a long road can say more about a place than six views from a window.
b : What's it say? | Which stone would you choose?
a : Whether folk have money for repairs, and whether water respects the edge. My soles can read both. | The one just before a doorway. There a street has to account for its effect indoors.

grown

story whiteedge [topic=work|memories]
  : I found a rag with exactly one white corner. I folded it with great care and put it aside for wiping a clean surface.
  : Reached for it later and found four equally grubby faces.
  b : Where was the white corner?
  : Inside my cleverest fold. A sound secret, though poor housekeeping.

story teawalk [topic=food|memories]
  : I took my tea on a walk to keep from sitting too long. Walked till I found a perfect patch of mist and then inspected my cup.
  : Tea cold, view warming up fast.
  b : Which did you keep?
  : The view. Drank the evidence against the tea before another wolf could offer a useful opinion.

story bootsole [topic=travel|memories]
  : A pebble tapped my heel all morning. Emptied my boot twice and found the lining clean. I sat down on a dry bollard for a better reckoning.
  : The pebble was stuck outside in the tread.
  b : How did it feel without it?
  : Oddly quiet. A long complaint can come to sound like part of your own natural step.

rule @fold
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Turn the spotless inch out and leave the rest in peace. | No need to display every stain in the length.

rule @work
when concept=bark self.job=none self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Sound fibres here under the old wearing crease. | Keep the soft strip away from the gritty wrap.

rule @boot
when concept=bark self.likes=new_boots
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A dry boot tongue is a luxury you feel all day. | Soft seam first, handsome leather after.

rule @tea
when concept=bark self.dislikes=cold_tea
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Catch the heat before a good cup loses its manners. | Cold tea sets my teeth to complaining.

dlg resident.hub : I've a clean little patch of the day to spare. Speak your piece.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you know which bit of my cloth is on public view.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Dark hides the stains without improving the material a jot.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : My pockets stay folded. You can ask your business from there.
dlg resident.job [self.job=none self.working=yes] : I sort cloth and look for the sound bit a careless hand would put aside.
dlg resident.job : Whatever earns a walk in boots with a clean lining interests me.
dlg resident.bye : Save one dry square against the road's last soggy turning.

graft resident.hub
choice What's folded into that strip of cloth? -> inwardrag
node inwardrag
say Nothing you'd pay money to see. There's one clean square inside for a gritty eyelid or fingers about to touch a good piece of cheese.
free
choice Why keep the worn side showing? -> outsidewear
choice I'll respect the fold. -> hub
node outsidewear
say Because the outer skin takes the weather. And nobody has yet tried to buy this sorry-looking rag while the sound patch stays out of sight.
choice That's a sensible private corner. -> hub
choice I'll get on with my walking. -> bye
